  "name": "Example: Finding the Image of an Object Under a Combination of Linear Transformations",
  "problem": "Consider the linear transformation that acts on vectors in $\\mathbb{R}^2$ as follows (in the order given):\n\n- it rotates vectors by $90^\\circ$ clockwise about the origin, and then\n\n- stretches the result by a scale factor of $2$ in the $y$-direction.\n\nWhat is the image of the unit square shown below under the action of this linear transformation?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062905/assets/e966d34d56ae25deb6bbf5849e813493c51730981031955e6833fd04d9ec1e2a.png)",
  "worked_solution": "First, we apply the rotation of $90^\\circ$ clockwise:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062905/assets/4da9df5bb1487aa693d9301c4a4901394da332197328637deef671a2bc59d204.png)\n\nThen, we apply the stretch by a scale factor of $2$ in the $y$-direction:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062905/assets/f400e267f38f4624d64e3a1899f9bbed3ba69996f1cf846ccc59e06e9eb5f35e.png)",
